      <div type="clause" n="24">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 24</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="62" ed="#liebermann"/>XXII. Gif neat mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.2"/> gewundige, weorpe ðæt neat to honda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.28"/> oððe foreðingie.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.29"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="62" ed="#liebermann"/>XXII. Gif monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.2-2"/> neat mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.2-2"/> gewundige, weorpe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.13"/> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> neat to honda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.2-2"/> oþþe foreþingie.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.14"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="62" ed="#liebermann"/>Be nytena misdædu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>. Gyf neat man gewundige, weorpe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> neat to handa oððe foreðingie.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="63" ed="#liebermann"/>Si alicuius animal hominem uulneret<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.19"/>, reddatur ipsum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.20"/> animal uel inde componatur.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_24.lnote.oe.21"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="74" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be nytena misdædum.] Gif neat<ptr type="editorNote" n="18" target="#Af_24.attnote.fn.18"/> mon gewundige, weorpe ðæt neat to honda oððe foreðingie.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="28" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="320" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXII} Gif neat mon gewundige, weorpe ðæt neat to honda oððe foreðingie.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="63" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_24.lnote.de.1"/> ein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_24.lnote.de.2"/> Rind einen Menschen verwundet, liefere [der Eigenthümer ihm] das Rind aus oder begleiche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_24.lnote.de.3"/> für dasselbe [die Zahlung an ihn].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If an ox wounds a person, let [the owner] hand the ox over [to him] or settle [the payment to him] for it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="75" ed="#attenborough"/>If a beast injures a man, [its owner] must hand over the beast [to the injured man], or come to terms [with him].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="413" ed="#whitelock"/>If a neat wounds a man, [the owner] is to hand over the neat, or to make terms.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="321" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a beast should wound someone, let [the owner] turn that beast over [to the wounded person] or let him settle [with the wounded person].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="321"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-21">Af El 21</ref> <quote>In MP §31 (derived from Exodus and thus of perhaps limited relevance) an ox who kills someone is slain by stoning</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-de <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> handa <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-de So; handa Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">forð. <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">forð. So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">erstes</hi> e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">first e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> foregeþ.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to foregeþ.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-raverit <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-raverit T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sibi illud <hi rend="italic">Or;</hi> i. a. <hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sibi illud Or; i. a. lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">secundum weram <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">secundum weram added by Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sachbeschädigung durch Vieh bei Ine 40. 42 ergänzt Af durch Menschenverwundung. — Er bestimmt hier deutlich anderes als <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> El 21. — <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Tierstrafe 1. 2; Rind 3a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Af supplements the damage to property by livestock in Ine 40. 42 with the wounding of persons. — Here he clearly lays down something different from <hi rend="italic">above</hi> El 21. — <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Tierstrafe 1. 2; Rind 3a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘jemandes’ fügen H Q zu</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H Q add ‘someone’s’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_24.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘stehe dafür ein’; denn geringste Wundenbusse überstieg den Wert des Rindes; Verletzter mochte das Tier nicht haben wollen und nahm lieber 30 Silberpfennige; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Ochs 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘be answerable for it’; for the smallest compensation for a wound exceeded the value of the ox; the injured man might not want the animal and preferred to take 30 silver pennies; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Ochs 1</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_24.attnote.fn.18" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope></bibl><label>neat</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">monnes neat</hi>. H.</seg></note>
      </div>
